    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26mksCEt6KEG7sXwPqeNpNV)_\n\nNew module `sp-refile` (doc `docs/tangles/funct/sp-refile.org`, tangled `sp-refile.el`) with one command, `sp-refile` (`C-x s t`, `C-c C-w` in Org):\n\n- On a heading it asks \"Refile to\" with one list: headings of the current note (the `org-refile` case), `[New note: own file]` (calls `sp-split-leave-parents`, so the #240 `- seealso ::` handling is unchanged) or `[Another note...]` (pick a note, then a heading or the top of it).\n- Before the first heading (or `C-u C-u`) it merges the whole note under a heading of another note: title becomes the heading, filetags its tags, the `:ID:` stays so links still resolve, then the old file is deleted after confirmation.\n- The copy is saved in the target before the source is removed.\n\nDecisions to check:\n- `vulpea-merge` is not in this repo or the container's Vulpea, so the merge is built from Org functions only.\n- `sp-split-leave-parents` stays as the split engine (code and tests untouched); `sp-refile` requires it. I did not move its 650 lines.\n- `C-x s t` now runs `sp-refile` (autoload and binding in `sp-org-base`); `sp-move-region-to-heading` (loose text, `M-a`) is untouched.\n\nTesting: 4 ERT tests (`tests/sp-refile-test.el`) pass in Emacs 29.3 batch with Vulpea/Denote stubbed. The prompts, the split path, merge deletion and the real Vulpea database were not run.\n\nBranch is the session's `claude/project-thread-rbj71z`, not number-prefixed, as the number was not known beforehand.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9YrF2wVqdAm7xCdTx)_",
